  "body": "Obsidian Skills now has a skill for Obsidian Headless, so agents can sync and publish vaults without the desktop app. The plugin also installs in Gemini CLI.\n\nIf you installed from the Claude Code marketplace, run `claude plugin update obsidian@obsidian-skills`.\n\n### Plugin\n\n- Added a Gemini CLI extension: `gemini extensions install https://github.com/obsidianmd/obsidian-skills`.\n\n### Skills\n\n- Headless: added a skill for `ob`, the Obsidian Headless CLI, to sync and publish vaults from the command line. It asks the user to type passwords and runs `publish` with `--dry-run` first (#75, #155).\n- Bases: added kanban views and `groupOrder` (#153), and documented the `note.` prefix that `displayName` needs in `properties` (#84).\n- Obsidian CLI: on WSL, call `Obsidian.com` instead of `Obsidian.exe` so output isn't lost (#96).\n\nThanks @catlee, @bencharoenwong, @hst368 and @citizen204!\n",
  "mentions_count": 4
